course: dictionary
lesson: 14045
title: Manufacturing: making goods in factories
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Manufacturing means making goods in large numbers, usually in a factory. As a noun, it is the whole business of making things. As a verb, to manufacture means to make things in a factory. «Car manufacturing needs many workers and big machines.»
explain: You can use context clues to work out the meaning. «The factory is manufacturing phones for the whole country.» Phones are goods, and a factory making them in big numbers fits the meaning of manufacturing. Check by swapping in a simple word: «The factory is making phones for the whole country.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Manufacturing is one kind of industry. Farming grows food, services such as shops and doctors help people, and manufacturing makes things. Many towns grew up around a factory, because workers needed homes and shops close by.
fact: Manufacturing means making goods in large numbers, usually in factories.
fact: Manufacturing is one type of industry, along with farming and services.
fact: As a noun, manufacturing is the business of making things; as a verb, «manufacturing» means making things in a factory.
fact: A factory where goods are made is often called a manufacturing plant.
fact: In maths problems, manufacturing costs are the money spent to make goods, and output per hour is how many items are made in one hour.
exercise: «The factory is manufacturing phones for the whole country.» What does manufacturing mean here? | Delivering letters to people | Repairing phones at home | Selling phones in a shop | *Making goods in a factory
exercise: Which phrase names a factory where goods are made? | Bus stop | *Manufacturing plant | Village green | Quiet library
exercise: Farming, services and ___ are the three kinds of industry in this lesson. | singing | reading | sleeping | *manufacturing
test: «Many towns grew up around car manufacturing.» What does this tell you? | Towns were built only for holidays | *Factories making cars helped the towns grow | Cars were sold in the park | People stopped making cars in the towns
test: In a maths problem, what are manufacturing costs? | The time a school day takes | Money earned from selling goods in a shop | The number of workers who go on holiday | *Money spent on making goods
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to the verb manufacture in «They are manufacturing new bikes»? | *produce | forget | relax | borrow
